# BMS operating mode transitions and hysteresis
**Review ID**: core-12
**Category**: core
**Date**: 2026-05-26
[0m
The review is written to `docs/reviews/core/core-12-bms-modes.md` (183 lines, 8 findings).

A key scope clarification: the reviewed file `bms.rs` implements a **Battery** Management System that dispatches charge/discharge setpoints, not a Building Management System with HVAC modes and temperature setpoints. The thermal/HVAC actor is `ideal_thermostat.rs`. The review was adapted accordingly.

**Summary of findings:**

| Severity | Count | Key Issues |
|----------|-------|------------|
| High | 2 | Zero hysteresis on all within-mode charge/discharge/idle transitions (Finding 1); no minimum dwell time enforcement (Finding 2) |
| Medium | 4 | Implicit mode priority via nesting (Finding 3); hardcoded DR threshold at 2x (Finding 4); inconsistent power caps across modes (Finding 5); static mode assignment with no runtime switching (Finding 6) |
| Low | 2 | Ambiguous TOU threshold behavior when percentiles overlap (Finding 7); `bms_action_code` returns -1 for Hold actions (Finding 8) |
